      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data Manipulation Language (DML) Commands\n    1. Different ways of insertion\n        - Inserting with specificied columns - If you want to add values only in a specific set of columns then, you need to pass `NULL`\nas a value for other column.\n        - Inserting from another table - Dont write `VALUES`\n        - If you are inserting just one record use `VALUE` otherwise use `VALUES`\n\n    2. The `UPDATE` and `DELETE` commands results reflect over entire dataset if there is no `WHERE` clause.\n\n    3. SELECT is a DQL/DML command\n    \n    4. Creating new column with default values\n        SELECT  *, 'samsung' AS 'phone'\n        FROM table_name;\n\n    → `DEFAULT` and `AUTO INCREMENT` checks ",
      "fontSize": 15.666434580269096,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data Manipulation Language (DML) Commands\n    1. Different ways of insertion\n        - Inserting with specificied columns - If you want to add values only in a specific set of columns then, you need to pass `NULL` as a value for other column.\n        - Inserting from another table - Dont write `VALUES`\n        - If you are inserting just one record use `VALUE` otherwise use `VALUES`\n\n    2. The `UPDATE` and `DELETE` commands results reflect over entire dataset if there is no `WHERE` clause.\n\n    3. SELECT is a DQL/DML command\n    \n    4. Creating new column with default values\n        SELECT  *, 'samsung' AS 'phone'\n        FROM table_name;\n\n    → `DEFAULT` and `AUTO INCREMENT` checks ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
